      priceMovement: "Bitcoin\'s price is expected to experience downward pressure and increased volatility in the immediate aftermath of such a large theft. The extent and duration of the price drop will depend on the market\'s reaction, Binance\'s response, and broader market sentiment. BNB\'s price would likely also decline due to its direct link to Binance\'s reputation.",
      onChainMetrics: "A large theft would be visible on-chain through the movement of stolen Bitcoin. Analysts would track these movements to identify potential liquidation attempts, new wallet addresses, or transfers to mixers. Increased on-chain activity related to withdrawals from exchanges could also be observed as users move funds to self-custody.",
      whaleActivity: "Whale activity might increase, either through large sell-offs by entities anticipating further price drops or strategic accumulations by those seeing a buying opportunity in the dip. Tracking large wallet movements post-theft is crucial for understanding market sentiment.",
      institutionalAdoption: "A major security breach like this could temper the pace of institutional adoption, as large institutions prioritize security, regulatory clarity, and risk management. It reinforces their concerns about the nascent nature of the crypto market\'s infrastructure.",
      regulatoryDevelopments: "This incident will undoubtedly accelerate regulatory discussions and calls for stricter oversight globally. Regulators like the SEC, FinCEN, and equivalent bodies in other jurisdictions will likely push for mandatory cybersecurity audits, proof-of-reserves, and enhanced consumer protection measures for crypto exchanges.",
      ecosystemGrowth: "While a setback, the incident could paradoxically contribute to the long-term growth and maturity of the ecosystem by forcing a focus on security. It might spur innovation in decentralized security solutions and self-custody tools, ultimately making the ecosystem more resilient.",
